<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Pickpockets</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 0)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> pickpocket &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>The pickpocket skill enables you to steal money from another living being.
When you try to pickpocket, your pick pocket skill, dexterity and brain and a
roll are compared to the target's brain and dexterity (and their own pick
pocket skill, if they are a player). The better your skill, the bigger the
handful of coins you take.
</p><p>A bad failure gets you caught red-handed with nothing to show for it. A
near miss gets you the coins, but the target sees you take them. Either way
it is a crime, you lose any invisibility, and the target may attack
you. A small failure gets you
nothing, but nobody notices. If your pick pocket is successful you still
risk that any bystanders see your crime even if the target didn't.
</p><p>You need at least one hand free, and you can't do it while fighting. You
can only pick a player's pocket if both of you have signed the book of
blood (see <a cmd='#'>Help Book of Blood</a>). Practising it needs dexterity 20.
</p><p>Example:
</p>
<pre> &gt; pickpo city guard
</pre>
<p>If you're good at picking pockets, this is a fast way to get cash and also a
way to spend some quality time in jail. Not to mention, a horde of blood thirsty
enemies. 
</p><p>Picking pockets is considered a crime, and few MUD'ers will help a thief in
trouble. Some will not help a thief at all. 
</p><p>Do notice that the command is in one word. Also note, that if you just type
'pick' then it is the pick lock command.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Stealing</a>
